Data Model JSON Schema:
[
  {
    "$defs": {
      "Rating": {
        "description": "A discretized rating on a 5-level integer scale from 1 to 5.\n\n`Rating` is the integer, Likert-style counterpart of `Score`: instead\nof a float between 0.0 and 1.0, the language model picks one of five\nwhole numbers, 1 (worst) to 5 (best). Because `Rating` is both an `int`\nand an `Enum`, the JSON schema constrains the model to exactly those\nfive values while Python code can use the value in arithmetic\ndirectly (e.g. averaging several ratings, or dividing by 5 to get a\nscore between 0.2 and 1.0).\n\nReach for `Rating` when you want the familiar \"rate this from 1 to 5\"\nframing (star ratings, Likert surveys, rubric grades), and for `Score`\nor `FineScore` when you want a normalized float.\n\nThe labels are the spelled-out numbers `ONE` (1) through `FIVE` (5).\n\nExample:\n\n```python\nimport synalinks\n\nclass Review(synalinks.DataModel):\n    rating: synalinks.Rating = synalinks.Field(\n        description=\"Overall quality of the answer, from 1 (worst) to 5 (best)\",\n    )\n\n# Rating values are real ints, usable in arithmetic.\nassert synalinks.Rating.FOUR == 4\nnormalized = synalinks.Rating.FOUR / 5  # 0.8\n```",
        "enum": [
          1,
          2,
          3,
          4,
          5
        ],
        "title": "Rating",
        "type": "integer"
      }
    },
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "description": "The questions a decision model answers about a ticket.",
    "properties": {
      "is_billing": {
        "description": "Is the ticket about billing?",
        "title": "Is Billing",
        "type": "boolean"
      },
      "urgency": {
        "description": "How urgent is the ticket?",
        "enum": [
          "low",
          "medium",
          "high"
        ],
        "title": "Urgency",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "frustration": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/Rating",
        "description": "How frustrated is the customer, from 1 (calm) to 5 (angry)?"
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "is_billing",
      "urgency",
      "frustration"
    ],
    "title": "Triage",
    "type": "object"
  }
]

